msgid ""
"[[quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-max-overdraft]] [.property-path]##link:#quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-max-overdraft[`+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-overdraft+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-overdraft+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"The number of requests per key that a replica may admit without holding permits, per emission interval (`window / permits`), while it claims a chunk from the store. `0` is strict: a request that finds no chunk waits for the claim, at most the store timeout (`quarkus.http.rate-limit.store-timeout`, or `quarkus.http.rate-limit.redis.timeout` for the `redis` store). Above `0` is optimistic: up to this many requests per emission interval are admitted at once and settled with the claim; when they are used up, or for a while after the store refused a claim, requests wait as in strict mode. Admissions that the store then refuses got through over the limit; they are forgiven, and counted. Between 0 and a static limit's burst; capped to the selected burst for resolved limits. Only valid with `lease-size`.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_RULES__RULE__MAX_OVERDRAFT+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr " link:#quarkus-http-rate-limit_quarkus-http-rate-limit-rules-rule-max-overdraft[quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-overdraft] config_property_copy_button:quarkus.http.rate-limit.rules.\"rule\".max-overdraft[]"

